{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Restoration attempt 2026-08-06 — STILL BLOCKED, no supported write path exists\n\nRe-measured the incident set against the current store and attempted the restoration.\n**0 edges restored. 59 remain outstanding.** Recording exactly what was tried.\n\n### 1. Map re-verified against the current store (AC1 — measurement half)\n\nLoaded all 63 children from `rebar list --include-archived` and compared each one's\ncurrent `parent_id` to the map in the comment above:\n\n* **63/63 children still exist** in the store (0 missing, 0 deleted).\n* **59 are parentless** (`parent_id` null/empty) — matches the ticket's count exactly.\n* **4 already hold the mapped parent** — `437c-dd9d-9e65-46e7`, `6758-26b8-c9ea-4c5d`,\n  `bf03-73bf-b66a-4c84`, `f2f3-9cb1-335b-4e31`. These are exactly the 4 marked\n  `[RESTORED]`.\n* **0 children hold some *other* parent** — nothing has drifted to a third value, so the\n  map is still an accurate description of the outstanding work.\n* The 59 outstanding edges point at **18 distinct parents, and all 18 are `closed`**\n  (17 `story`, 1 `bug` — `03b0-2290-f4f3-47a8`). Not one is open/in_progress.\n\nDistinct closed parents: `03b0-2290-f4f3-47a8`, `096c-0dc3-25cc-4513`,\n`0e35-6632-41e5-4ee6`, `0ee8-08de-bf0f-45ec`, `297d-a233-ce1b-4484`,\n`2c14-fa5f-1228-4e02`, `3c55-2af3-0c9c-4b11`, `4014-d34b-d312-45d3`,\n`5a52-054b-4b1b-48e4`, `60ce-29c1-58be-4648`, `64ef-c743-b012-40e8`,\n`7f86-d935-3742-476a`, `87ab-a676-622b-4b44`, `9f84-bc2c-6f8b-4b09`,\n`affe-2b42-4ee4-4e12`, `da8a-75f5-ccb2-4b5f`, `e6c2-6a04-34d7-4cb5`,\n`eb58-e71d-ec90-4b00`.\n\n### 2. `rebar edit --parent` — refused, verbatim\n\n```\n$ rebar edit 0426-5184-652a-44d4 --parent=096c-0dc3-25cc-4513\nError: cannot re-parent to closed ticket '096c-0dc3-25cc-4513'. Reopen the parent first with: ticket transition 096c-0dc3-25cc-4513 closed open\n```\n\nSource of the refusal: `_resolve_new_parent` in `src/rebar/_commands/composer.py`\n(the `status not in (\"open\", \"in_progress\")` branch). There is **no override**:\n\n* `rebar edit --help` lists no `--force` / `--allow-closed-parent` flag, and the word\n  `force` does not appear anywhere in `composer.py`.\n* The library route is not a bypass — `rebar.edit_ticket()` calls the same\n  `composer.edit_core`, so it hits the identical cascade.\n* `rebar` has **no `parent` subcommand** (confirmed against `rebar --help`).\n  `5992-f317-e05e-42f7`, which would add it with `--force`, is **still status `idea`**.\n\n### 3. The reopen → re-parent → re-close route is NOT a safe substitute\n\nThe error text suggests reopening the parent. Deliberately **not** done, because on this\nproject it trades a data-loss bug for a worse one. `rebar.toml` has BOTH close gates on:\n\n* `require_completion_verification_for_close = true`\n* `require_plan_review_for_close = true`\n\nSo re-closing a reopened parent needs a **current execution-phase plan-review\nattestation** plus an LLM completion verification. Probed a representative parent\n(`60ce-29c1-58be-4648`, the largest, 9 children):\n\n```\n$ rebar review-plan 60ce-29c1-58be-4648 --status\n{\"ok\": false, \"verdict\": \"unsigned\", \"reason\": \"no certified plan-review attestation\n (signature: unsigned; ticket has no signature)...\", \"verified_at_sha\": null, \"signed_at\": null}\n```\n\nThese are long-closed legacy stories with no attestation, so each re-close would require\na fresh LLM plan-review PASS on a story written before the current criteria existed —\nlikely BLOCK. Executing this route means **18 reopens** and, on any failure, **closed\nparents stranded in `open`** — corrupting 18 more tickets' status on top of the 59 lost\nedges, plus ~95 write events of Jira reconcile churn. The only way through would be\n`--force-close`, i.e. bypassing the gate 18 times. That is not a supported write path;\nit is the escape hatch, and it is a human operator's call, not an agent's.\n\n### 4. Status against this ticket's acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] map verified against the store (all 63 accounted for; 59 outstanding, 4 restored, 0 drifted)\n- [ ] **a supported write path exists for re-parenting onto a closed parent — STILL FALSE.**\n      This is the hard blocker. `5992-f317-e05e-42f7` is still `idea`.\n- [ ] 59 edges restored — 0 done, blocked on the above\n- [ ] post-restore sweep — not reachable\n- [ ] confirm a later reconcile pass does not re-clear — not reachable\n\n### What would unblock this\n\nImplement `5992-f317-e05e-42f7` (a `parent` verb, or an `edit --parent --force`, that\nskips only the closed-parent branch of `_resolve_new_parent` while keeping the\nexistence and cycle checks). That single change turns this into a 59-line scripted\nreplay of the map above. Restoring a historical parent edge onto an intentionally\nclosed parent is exactly the case the status check was never meant to cover, and the\nreopen/re-close workaround the error message advertises is unavailable wherever the\nplan-review + completion close gates are enforced.\n\nThis ticket stays **open**. No store writes were made by this attempt."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786078894691924001,"uuid":"907dc1ae-715f-4cc2-b01a-17bcbfc53b48"}